WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.725
Start in the service administrator's control tower: outstanding orders, active services and exceptions together in one view.

2
00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:17.664
Microsoft sign-in applies assigned roles. The access-token fallback gives new engineers service-operator permissions.

3
00:00:18.292 --> 00:00:26.770
Create a request for a registered enterprise. Choose the city, product and scenario, then send it for the enterprise's approval.

4
00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:37.380
Orders await enterprise approval. No agent starts provisioning before consent; administrators can inspect status or withdraw a request.

5
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:47.417
The order workspace brings service requests together. Open an order to follow its current stage, ownership, updates and execution history.

6
00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:57.608
Review route conflicts and change-window holds in the exception desk. Recovery does not override a decision reserved for a service
manager.

7
00:00:58.208 --> 00:01:08.480
Set up partner organisations and invite named contacts. Review account status and manage access without sharing administrator
credentials.

8
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:18.640
Open a partner account to maintain billing contacts and payment terms, inspect invoices, and record or reverse a simulated payment.

9
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:28.231
The shared inbox keeps delivery concerns and replies beside their orders, so the service team can resolve issues with context.

10
00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:39.498
Inspect the specialist workspaces: Validate checks the request, Decompose builds the plan, and Provision executes permitted service steps
through the boundary.

11
00:01:40.125 --> 00:01:50.225
Recover handles supported failures; Communicate prepares updates. Deployed Foundry workers use scoped tools, not unrestricted data
access.

12
00:01:50.833 --> 00:02:00.369
Separate operational orders from benchmarks. Review completion, fallout and agent timings to identify where the process needs
attention.

13
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:10.332
Repeatable synthetic scenarios compare outcomes and recovery. Their timings are not production commitments or measured carrier
performance.

14
00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:19.522
Governance exposes policy gates and audit records. Filter decisions by person and order, then export evidence for review.

15
00:02:20.125 --> 00:02:29.052
Customers track requests; partners manage assigned deliveries. The service team coordinates everything from the administrator's console.
